WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:02.190
Tuesday
October 24th

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:03.850
<i>It's possible that Oka Eri will come to your place.
Tuesday
October 24th</i>

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.560
<i>It's possible that Oka Eri will come to your place.</i>

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.360
<i>If you become unable to reset, please tell me.</i>

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.110
<i>Also, once you read this message,
delete it immediately.</i>

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:20.700
<i>I understand.</i>

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.710
<i>What are you doing now, Kei?</i>

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.460
<i>I was tidying up my room.</i>

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.800
<i>Have you finished what you had to do?</i>

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.800
<i>I'm done with most of it,
now I just have one more thing to do.</i>

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.140
<i>Will you be able to finish everything today?</i>

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.930
<i>Is it okay if I keep messaging you?</i>

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:48.400
It's been a while, Kei.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.280
Come in.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.900
It really has been ages.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.990
I wouldn't mind you coming more often.

00:00:55.990 --> 00:01:00.240
I also wouldn't mind that,
but I have a lot going on, you see.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:35.960
It's really nice and tidy here.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:38.010
Because I don't have much stuff.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.470
Also, I did some quick vacuuming earlier.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.850
I could have cleaned your room for you.

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.350
That would be kinda awkward.

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:48.180
Want a coffee or something?

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.980
Coffee does sound nice,

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.690
but I'd like to make some chicken curry first.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:55.110
I bought this just for that purpose.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.190
What is it?

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:58.690
Something you can't cook without.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:03.200
How is it?

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.620
Looks like something you'd wear in home ec class.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:10.210
I can imagine handing out
cookies you made looking like that.

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.040
What's that supposed to mean?

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.670
Does that mean I don't really look housewife-y?

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.550
It means you look like a normal girl.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:18.920
It suits you well.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:21.470
Sure, if you say so.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:24.140
Okay, let's make that chicken curry.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.730
I think I'll tell you a story.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:34.110
What kind of story will it be?

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.360
First, let's see...

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:40.360
A story of a certain ability user and his child.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.990
I hope abilities disappear soon.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.240
They won't.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:49.910
Because we're here, you see.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.960
Don't you want them to disappear, Dad?

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.960
Of course not.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:59.420
Our goal is to create a town where
abilities can exist without any issues.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.720
Why?

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.510
I used to hate abilities.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:07.600
They're useful, but there's
too many problems involved.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.480
I used to think it'd be wiser to get rid of them.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:11.140
Yeah.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:15.060
But I realized something when you were born.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.980
There's something to gain from our abilities.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:20.490
I want to make this town a place
where wonderful miracles happen.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.400
That's my goal.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.740
Miracles shouldn't happen!

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:28.080
People should be happy with their own power!

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.330
You're a very strong child.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:33.500
But I believe that a world
that allows people to be weak

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:37.040
is more rightful than a world
where everyone is strong.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.380
A place where weak people
are saved by handy miracles

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.630
couldn't be wrong, don't you think?

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:46.140
I'm sorry.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:48.930
I'm making you go through something sad.

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.100
I don't really care.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:55.600
I can't allow anyone to become
a sacrifice to abilities, though.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:56.690
Masamune...

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:00.440
I'm sure I can't save you, Dad.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:04.780
But I want to make sure
no one like you is ever born again.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.870
You have a very strong sense of rightfulness.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.660
But I want you to listen and understand.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.210
I really love you.

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:17.790
You're my pride and my hope.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:21.550
But I'm sometimes scared.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:22.460
Why?

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:25.170
Because you're a very strong child.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.890
You right everything that is wrong.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.550
What's scary about it?

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:33.390
We're way weaker than you might think.

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:35.560
We're weak, and so we make mistakes.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.230
But there's some happiness to gain from that.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:41.940
I'm sure you'd right even that, though.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.400
You're very strong.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.490
Now you need to learn how it is to be weak.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:49.780
What's there to gain from being weak?

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:53.910
Once you learn how it is to be weak,
you become more forgiving.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:57.080
There's no need to allow people to make mistakes.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.420
It's not about people. It's about yourself.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:04.420
People become kinder to accept themselves.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:08.130
Urachi... am I correct?

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:09.180
Who are you?

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:13.680
I've practically turned your father into stone...

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.770
I'm sorry.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.560
There's no need to apologize.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:22.770
What you did was right.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:24.360
Take pride in it.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:28.450
There was a need for my father
to continue using his ability forever.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:31.370
It's like you saved the world.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:35.240
If my father really believed that abilities are rightful,

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.830
he should have exposed them to the whole world.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.540
The reason he hid them from the world

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:43.040
is probably that he was aware of their dangers.

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:45.380
We can't pretend that wasn't it.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:49.010
Abilities won't save weak people.

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:50.470
It's the opposite.

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:54.970
If we want to protect the weak,
we should get rid of abilities.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:59.810
That's Urachi Masamune's story.

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:01.940
Now I understand.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:06.320
Urachi hates abilities with every fiber of his being.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.440
Are you okay with that?

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:09.780
No, I'm not.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:12.530
I love Sakurada's abilities.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.990
Yeah, seems good.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.410
We should move onto the main topic now.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:22.960
That sounds as if this story
wasn't related to it at all.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:24.590
Of course it wasn't.

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:28.090
I couldn't care less about Urachi.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:32.430
It was just a way to kill time
while making the chicken curry.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.180
That's mean.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:36.350
Could I borrow your shower?

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.350
So you really were planning to take a shower?

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:45.730
That's why I'm here.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.410
<i>Could we have dinner together tomorrow?</i>

00:07:58.700 --> 00:07:59.750
<i>Of course.</i>

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.710
<i>I'll look for a good restaurant.</i>

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.330
<i>Thinking of anything particular?</i>

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.340
Come here. To the door.

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:07.880
Why?

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.380
Didn't I promise you?

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:12.630
That I'd tell you everything I was keeping secret.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:14.260
I can hear it later.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.680
You should take your time washing yourself.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.720
There's nothing to wash.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:21.930
I took a bath right before coming here.

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:25.860
Why would you take a bath before taking a shower?

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:27.650
It's very simple.

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:32.320
I couldn't go meet with the person I love being all sweaty, could I?

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:36.870
What are you going to tell me?

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:38.120
What do you want to know?

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:40.120
I'll answer any question.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.120
Say, Souma.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.080
Why did you die?

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.210
Haven't I answered that already before?

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:51.920
I didn't want to become like the Witch.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:54.800
Trapped by the Bureau forever, you know.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:58.510
You could have just left Sakurada two years ago.

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:03.270
I had to stay in Sakurada
to execute my plan, you see.

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.350
That doesn't change anything.

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:09.020
You could have left and come back two years later.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:10.650
The reason...

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:15.070
The real reason you died was to stop
being Souma Sumire, wasn't it?

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:18.660
I've been thinking about it all night.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.910
I'm still thinking about it.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:24.210
But I can't see any other reason you could have had.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:29.960
That's why the instructions I've been getting
were from the Souma Sumire who died two years ago.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.920
And that's not you.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:35.590
Because you don't consider yourself Souma Sumire.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.760
You haven't told me anything.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:40.720
That's correct, Kei.

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:45.060
Urachi asked me this question:

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:47.730
"Will you try to foil my plan?"

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:52.480
I had to answer that I wouldn't.

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:54.570
In front of Index, you see.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:59.740
I had to say "No, I won't do anything",
and it had to be the truth.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:02.280
So you died as a preparation for that.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:03.620
Yeah.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:07.120
The one opposing Urachi's plan is Souma Sumire.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:10.630
The one giving you instructions
was also Souma Sumire.

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:14.960
I don't consider myself Souma Sumire, though.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:17.550
I'm her swampman.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:21.100
Just a system without a name or identity.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:24.100
That's why I could honestly say
that I wouldn't do anything.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:27.350
Urachi is certainly something,
but he missed this one little thing.

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:31.310
If he'd used "Souma Sumire"
instead of "you" in his question,

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:33.770
I would have had to tell him everything.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:35.230
I had to bet on that.

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:40.110
But I made sure that he wouldn't be able
to call me by my name before that.

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:45.740
I helped him on the condition he
wouldn't investigate into my identity.

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:48.620
How can you talk about it like that?

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:51.880
That's because, you see...

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.880
You're the only one who understands me, Kei.

00:10:55.630 --> 00:11:00.090
I managed to deceive Urachi,
but I'd never be able to deceive you.

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:02.850
You think a lot about Misora,

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:07.470
but I know that you thought even more about me.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:08.600
Souma Sumire!

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.600
You're such a fool.

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:14.980
I'm not Souma Sumire anymore.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:19.030
I'm just an android without a name
that resembles a human.

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:22.160
It must be from Haruki.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:35.000
You can reply, you know.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:38.460
I'm talking with you right now.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:40.130
Haruki can wait.

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:41.180
Is that so?

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:44.140
Such trust.

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:45.390
Souma.

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.010
What are you trying to achieve?

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:50.560
You're asking now?
Don't you already know the answer well?

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:54.360
My goal is to foil Urachi Masamune's plan.

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:56.730
No, not mine.

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:59.530
It's the goal of Souma Sumire,
who died two years ago.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:00.990
You're lying.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:03.160
You were cooperating with Urachi.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:05.450
It was Souma Sumire's choice

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:08.870
whose time to rewind when
to make accidents happen.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:13.120
You had to accelerate Urachi's plan.

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:16.630
A reset can only erase three days worth of time.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:19.760
If his plan didn't fit within that time,
we wouldn't be able to resolve it.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.760
You gave me a chance.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.090
I was only after efficiency.

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:31.180
It was the most efficient to use you
to foil Urachi Masamune's plan.

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:33.690
Efficient? No way.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:36.190
Your actions are far from being efficient.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:39.110
If foiling Urachi's plan was your sole goal,

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:42.070
you could have told me everything
at the very beginning.

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:46.030
That way, I could have acted way more accurately.

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:49.330
It was to deal with Index's ability...

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:52.290
Didn't you already die two years ago for that?

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:55.000
Even if you couldn't tell me now,

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:58.040
your self two years ago shouldn't
have had any restrictions.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:02.300
There wouldn't be any problems
even if you had told me sooner.

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:07.680
You had an entirely different reason
to keep all of this secret.

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:12.930
Two days ago, I was truly happy.

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:18.610
I was able to talk with Haruki about something
really important on the school roof.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:21.030
I'm sure we still have a long way to go.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:23.690
But something had definitely changed.

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:29.910
I think I hadn't ever been
that happy in my life before.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:33.500
And yesterday too,
when I picked up trash with Haruki,

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:37.080
when we ate crepes together,
went shopping together at that supermarket,

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:40.420
it was so fun, I couldn't have been happier.

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:44.470
Thank you, Souma.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:47.550
You protected my happiness.

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:53.640
I mean... I didn't have any other choice.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.140
I'm stupid, aren't I?

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:58.020
Don't you think I'm a fool?

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:01.070
The reason I didn't say anything for so long

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:04.490
was to wait for the person I love

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:08.700
to tell another girl how much he loves her.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:12.910
<i>I never understood Souma's intentions.</i>

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:14.660
<i>I've always known that.</i>

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:17.460
<i>But only now, I understand.</i>

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:20.630
<i>She had to take a shower.</i>

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:24.550
<i>Because she knew she'd cry.</i>

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:36.060
You know, Kei. There's someone I absolutely hate.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:38.730
She's so unfair.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:40.980
She's the only one who doesn't suffer.

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:46.070
Pretending it's for your sake, she escapes
into a position where she doesn't get hurt.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:49.990
All the pain is forced onto me.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:52.240
She's the only one who has it easy.

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:55.040
Do you know who I'm talking about?

00:14:55.790 --> 00:15:00.790
She was so stupid, so selfish, and extremely weak.

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:04.800
Do you know who I'm talking about?

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:07.920
Please... I want you to...

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:11.300
I want you to forgive Souma Sumire.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:17.520
You really are the only one who understands me.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:22.190
I can't forgive her for creating me.

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:24.730
But you know, Kei...

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:28.530
I can't help being the same as her.

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:34.280
I'll always wish for your happiness alone.

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:46.300
How is it?

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:48.550
It's very good.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:50.970
It's also somehow nostalgic.

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:52.720
A lot of tomatoes,

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:55.970
and just a little bit of yogurt was the key.

00:15:56.260 --> 00:16:01.690
My mother used to add yogurt to make sure
it wouldn't be too spicy when I was young.

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:04.190
She kept reducing the amount,

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:07.860
but there was always a little bit of it in our curry.

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:10.030
But it's a bit different, isn't it?

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:12.450
That's true. Any particular reason?

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:14.740
No, there isn't.

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:17.200
I just couldn't recreate it.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:22.290
I used my ability many, many
times to make this curry.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:24.830
But no matter how hard I tried,

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:28.420
I couldn't find a future where
you'd say it tastes the same.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:30.630
That's so strange. I wonder why?

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:32.010
Who knows.

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:35.970
Even clairvoyance can't
compete with motherly love.

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:38.100
I'm sure that's the only reason.

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:40.600
Thank you.

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:42.020
It was really good.

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:43.230
But of course.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.270
I made it with lots of love.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:51.610
I've decided to protect abilities.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:53.450
To borrow your words,

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:56.160
I'm planning to rule over all abilities in Sakurada.

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:58.490
Like the MacGuffin was supposed to allow.

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:02.540
I'll rule over them, use them all as I please,

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:04.620
and proceed towards the goal

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:08.880
of making Sakurada's abilities
a miracle that brings happiness.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:10.670
I'm sure you'll do well.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:14.630
You're my protagonist, after all.

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:20.010
Can I leave the dishes to you?

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:20.760
Of course.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.560
I'll be leaving, then.

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:25.730
It'll start raining soon.

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:27.770
Could I borrow an umbrella, maybe?

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:29.650
When will it rain?

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:31.480
In about ten minutes.

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:32.230
I see.

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:36.820
Should I go with you?

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:38.410
No, I'm fine.

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:41.540
It's dangerous for a girl
to walk outside at night alone.

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:44.960
Only if it's a normal girl who doesn't see the future.

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.710
Well, goodbye.

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:48.080
That won't do.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:48.790
Huh?

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:54.050
You've only said "goodbye" to me once before.

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:56.930
Two years ago, at the bus stop in the rain.

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:01.680
See you again then, Kei.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:10.690
Come in.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:18.490
We're from the Bureau.

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:19.780
What about my mother?

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:22.950
Another member of the Bureau
is explaining the matter to her.

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:25.200
What is it?

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:28.710
It's a bit difficult to explain.

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:30.210
It won't take long, though.

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:34.710
If you don't move, there won't be any problems.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.720
Look...

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:42.470
We're done already.

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:48.140
She still alive?

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:50.770
Of course.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:54.820
She was just sleeping during
the time I rewound her to.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:57.530
Two years and seven months ago.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.450
What are you doing now?

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:05.080
Oh, it's nothing.

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:08.460
Okay, I need to be going now.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:10.170
I need you to do me a favor.

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:12.420
Well, of course you do.

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:15.130
An ambulance will come here soon.

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:17.380
They'll quarantine her in the hospital.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:19.050
And?

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:21.180
I want you to accompany them.

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:23.350
Once she wakes up,

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:25.970
could you make her forget how to use her ability?

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:28.560
And will this really be a win against Asai?

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.140
Of course.

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:32.270
He'd hate that more than anything else.

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:34.150
I'm counting on you.

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:48.290
Rewinding Haruki Misora to before
she met Asai Kei for the first time...

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:52.290
I wonder how much of this
Asai was expecting to happen.

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:57.550
Oka Eri.

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:01.260
You're cooperating with Urachi, aren't you?

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:02.880
Asai's voice?

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:05.550
I'm sure you don't know their goal, though.

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:08.140
Listen, what they're planning to do

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:11.060
is to erase all the abilities from Sakurada.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:13.690
You don't have to believe me.

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:17.860
If you doubt them even the slightest, please.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:20.570
Just don't take away Haruki Misora's reset ability.

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:22.700
Please, Oka Eri.

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:24.700
I've been driven into a corner.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:26.700
I need you to help me.

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:31.040
He's so unfair.

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:33.170
"I need you to help me" is against the rules.

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:39.420
Would there be any better way
of winning than helping him?

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:48.220
Is it painful to look at them?

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:50.810
Yes, of course.

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:52.810
You shouldn't care this much.

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:54.980
You did the right thing.

00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:56.270
Take pride in it.

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:59.110
Yes, I'm aware.

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:03.110
Is it not painful for you to meet them?

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:04.740
Of course it is.

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:08.830
But I'm meeting my mother for
the first time in ages, so I'm also happy.

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:12.370
My mother turned into stone
eight years after my father...

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:14.750
The day I turned twenty,

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.710
you stopped her time with your ability.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:21.210
Today, she will live again.

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:23.510
She'll be human again.

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:25.340
It's a happy event.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:27.300
Please.

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:52.120
It's time to wake up from your long dream.

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:55.080
I'll reset Sakurada.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:57.460
Next Episode

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:58.920
I don't remember you.

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:00.130
Seems like today is the beginning of a new world.

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:02.000
Is it like the hypothesis that
the world began five minutes ago?

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:03.880
I've done a terrible thing to my mother and father.

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:05.260
I want you to remember everything.

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:06.260
Please, remember!

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:07.130
I can't.

00:22:07.130 --> 00:22:07.470
Haruki!

00:22:07.470 --> 00:22:09.090
I can't remember you!

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:10.350
It's time to reset!

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:21.360
On such a cold dark sky of grey

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:27.570
Rises the sun, which breathes life into it

00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:33.830
A scenery so plain and so mundane

00:22:34.120 --> 00:22:43.420
And yet it seems to break my heart, it's so dear to me

00:22:44.300 --> 00:22:47.880
As the time never stops passing by

00:22:47.880 --> 00:22:50.260
You get lost while searching for

00:22:50.260 --> 00:22:54.140
Pure like the rays of a morning star

00:22:54.140 --> 00:22:57.060
What we all yearn for the most

00:22:57.060 --> 00:23:00.480
In what colors bliss is dyed

00:23:00.650 --> 00:23:03.110
Struggling against all your past mistakes

00:23:03.110 --> 00:23:06.150
At last from the answer you found kindness fills your heart

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:09.320
More beautiful than anything you know

00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:12.950
And you find it behind a dark veil of sadness

00:23:12.950 --> 00:23:15.450
If I closed my eyes and stopped my thoughts

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:17.200
If it were so simple to just

00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:20.210
Lock your own heart

00:23:20.210 --> 00:23:23.340
How lovely life would be

00:23:23.340 --> 00:23:28.590
But I believe you have the key

00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:34.930
To let my soul be free
